 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "One unit of about 151 s: the reciter joins 154 to 158. A moon for the calm drowsiness, wind for the suspicion, geometric for «إن الأمر كله لله», a house for «لو كنتم في بيوتكم», a door for the pardon, footsteps for travel, coins for what they gather. Nothing for the killed, the Shaytan or the battle. The hypocrites' claims (154:41-50, 156:17-23) are not glossed as statements. STAGING v4: 154 stays ambient: the battlefield of Uhud (the drowsiness came during the battle, the killed, «ما قتلنا هاهنا»). 155 stays ambient: those who fled the battle and the Shaytan. 157-158 stay ambient: being killed or dying in His path, the Gathering. 156: the disbelievers sit in their town (Al-Muyassar: وأقاموا معنا) and speak about their brothers; one traveller sets out on «ضربوا في الأرض» (both tafsirs: travel for trade or livelihood) and is gone before the raiding and the deaths are named, so no one is seen dying; the speakers wring their hands on «حسرة»."
 },
